# Frontend Architecture

## Structure

```
frontend/src/
├── assets/
├── components/
│   ├── common/   Button, Input, Select, SearchInput, Badge, StatusBadge, Loader, Toast, Pagination, Dropdown,
│   │             LoadingState, EmptyState, ErrorState, PageHeader, Breadcrumb, DatePicker, FormField
│   ├── layout/   Sidebar, Navbar
│   ├── forms/
│   ├── tables/   DataTable
│   ├── modals/   Modal, ConfirmationModal
│   ├── cards/    Card, StatCard, ChartCard
│   └── charts/
├── pages/        auth/, admin/, member/
├── layouts/
├── routes/       ProtectedRoute, route definitions
├── services/     apiClient.js, authService.js, memberService.js, membershipService.js,
│                 attendanceService.js, reportService.js, announcementService.js
├── hooks/        useAuth, useFetch, usePagination, useDebounce, useModal, useForm, useAttendance
├── context/
├── utils/        centralized date utility, formatters
├── constants/
├── config/
├── validations/
├── App.jsx
└── main.jsx
```

## Reusable components — one implementation, configured via props

Never create page-specific copies of Button, Modal, Table, Form, etc.
- **DataTable**: one system supporting columns, sorting, search, filtering, pagination, actions, empty/loading
  states and responsive behavior. Separate table implementations only when requirements genuinely differ.
- **Modals**: one reusable modal system with configurable content (Add/Edit Member, Delete Confirmation,
  Add/Edit Plan, Announcement).
- **States**: every API-driven page handles Loading, Success, Empty and Error using the shared
  `LoadingState`, `EmptyState`, `ErrorState` components — no custom per-page loading screens.
- **Notifications**: one centralized toast system; messages come from constants.
- **Dashboard**: built from `StatCard`, `ChartCard`, `ActivityList`, `DataTable`.

## Forms

Validate with shared validation schemas in `validations/`; show clear errors; prevent invalid submissions;
show loading state while submitting; disable duplicate submission; show success/error feedback; reset correctly.
Reuse common form components — never duplicate the member/plan/announcement forms.

## API layer

All HTTP calls go through `services/apiClient.js` (shared base URL, auth header, error normalization).
Feature services wrap endpoints from `constants/`. Never repeat fetch/axios configuration in components.
Only create a service when needed.

## Hooks & state

Check for an existing hook before creating one. Keep UI state, auth state, server data and form state separate.
Prefer local state; use context only for truly shared state (e.g. auth). No state-management library.
Use `useMemo`/`useCallback` only with a real reason.

## Search & pagination

Search is reusable (`SearchInput` + `useDebounce`), avoids unnecessary requests, and shows a clear empty state.
Pagination is reusable and reads defaults from constants — never hardcode page sizes in pages.

## Routing

Protected routes with role-based redirects. Unauthorized users are redirected appropriately.

```
/login
/admin/dashboard  /admin/members  /admin/payments  /admin/membership-plans  /admin/attendance
/admin/reports    /admin/announcements  /admin/settings  /admin/profile
/member/dashboard /member/profile /member/membership /member/attendance /member/announcements
```

Route paths are constants. Frontend protection is a UX layer only — the backend enforces authorization.

## Performance

Pagination, debounced search, lazy loading where appropriate, avoid unnecessary API calls.
